@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-hourly-rentals-sub-day-periods-on-the-hour-no-discount-no-new-validation-path-duplicated
+type: decision-log
+title: "Hourly rentals: sub-day periods on the hour, no discount, no new validation path duplicated"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and the desk could previously only rent by the whole
+UTC day (dl-001). The request adds an `hourlyPrice` to `addEquipment` and asks that "a rental shorter than
+a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's hourly price for each hour", and that "an
+item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour". The existing `wholeDaysBetween` validation
+(used by `quote`, `book` via `quote`, and `availability` per dl-002) had to grow to accept this second kind
+of period without duplicating validation or overlap logic across call sites.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Period resolution**: `wholeDaysBetween` is replaced by `resolvePeriod(start, end)`, which returns a
+  tagged `RentalPeriod` (`{ unit: 'day', amount, start, end }` or `{ unit: 'hour', amount, start, end }`).
+  A period resolves to whole days when both `start` and `end` are exactly UTC midnight and the duration is
+  a whole number of days (unchanged from dl-001). Otherwise, if the duration is strictly less than 24h and
+  both `start` and `end` fall exactly on the hour (zero minutes/seconds/milliseconds), it resolves to whole
+  hours. Any other shape (e.g. not on the hour, or a day-or-longer period not aligned to midnight) still
+  throws, preserving the existing "day-or-more rentals must be whole, midnight-aligned days" behaviour.
+- **No discount on hourly rentals**: the long-rental discount (dl-003) only triggers at `days >= 3`; since
+  an hourly period is by construction shorter than a day, it can never reach that threshold, so no explicit
+  exclusion was needed — `priceForPeriod` simply routes day periods through the existing `priceForDays`
+  (renamed from `priceFor`) and hour periods through `amount * item.hourlyPrice`, with no discount applied.
+- **Missing `hourlyPrice` is a pricing-time error, not a validation-time one**: `addEquipment` only
+  validates `hourlyPrice` when present (non-negative integer cents, like `dailyPrice`), since it is
+  optional. Whether an item *can* be rented by the hour is checked in `priceForPeriod`, at the point an
+  hourly period is actually priced, because that's the only place both the period's unit and the item are
+  available together; `quote` throws before `book` can create any booking, matching the existing
+  quote-before-book side-effect ordering.
+- **Single resolution point reused everywhere**: `quote`, `book` (through `quote`), and `availability` all
+  call `resolvePeriod` once; `availability` now also accepts hourly query periods, consistent with dl-002's
+  decision to keep period validation and overlap rules identical across all three operations.
+- **Two pre-existing tests revised, not removed**: two tests asserted that *any* non-whole-day period was
+  invalid; that's no longer true (a sub-day period on the hour is valid). Both were changed to exercise
+  periods that are still genuinely invalid (not aligned to the hour either), rather than being deleted,
+  per the testing directive's requirement to cover both the happy path and the error path for every
+  behaviour.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `quote`/`book`/`availability` share one notion of "valid period" and one overlap rule regardless of
+  granularity, so an hourly booking and a daily booking on the same item are compared correctly (e.g. a
+  2-hour booking ending at 13:00 does not block a daily booking starting the same day at midnight the next
+  day, and vice versa).
+- A rental that spans a day or more but isn't midnight-aligned (e.g. 30 hours starting at 10:00) is still
+  rejected; mixed day-plus-hours pricing was out of scope for this request and would need a new
+  `RentalPeriod` variant and pricing rule if ever required.
+- `priceForPeriod` is the one place that enforces "an item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the
+  hour"; a future caller that needs to check this ahead of calling `quote` would need its own helper, since
+  there is currently no separate "can this item be rented by the hour" query.
