@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+---
+id: task-004-allow-renting-equipment-by-the-hour
+type: task
+title: "Allow renting equipment by the hour"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Let customers rent equipment by the hour, not only by the whole day, since many visitors only want a
+board for an afternoon. `addEquipment` now also accepts an `hourlyPrice` (what one hour costs). A rental
+shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's hourly price for each hour.
+An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added an optional `hourlyPrice` field to `Equipment`, validated in `addEquipment` the same way as
+  `dailyPrice` (non-negative integer number of cents) when present.
+- Replaced the day-only period validation (`wholeDaysBetween`) with `resolvePeriod`, which accepts either
+  whole UTC days starting and ending at midnight (as before), or, for a period shorter than a day, whole
+  hours starting and ending on the hour. Any other period still throws.
+- Added `priceForPeriod`, which prices a day period with the existing long-rental discount logic
+  (`priceForDays`, formerly `priceFor`) or an hour period at `amount * item.hourlyPrice`, throwing if the
+  item has no `hourlyPrice`.
+- `quote`, `book` (via `quote`) and `availability` all go through `resolvePeriod`, so hourly periods are
+  quoted, booked and checked for availability/overlap consistently with day periods.
+- Wrote tests first (red, then green): hourly quoting and booking, rejecting hourly rentals on an item
+  without an hourly price, rejecting a period that is neither whole days nor whole hours, hourly overlap
+  and back-to-back booking, hourly `availability`, and `addEquipment` validation of `hourlyPrice`. Two
+  pre-existing tests that asserted *any* non-whole-day period was invalid were updated, since a sub-day
+  period on the hour is now valid; they now exercise genuinely invalid periods (or, for the `sail-1` case,
+  an item without an hourly price keeps that case accurate by also giving the item an `hourlyPrice` and a
+  non-hour-aligned time).
+- No discount applies to hourly rentals: the long-rental discount only ever triggers on `days >= 3`
+  (dl-003), which cannot be reached by a sub-day hourly rental.
+
+## Result
+
+`npm test` passes: 30/30 tests green.
